# Carvis engineering context

Carvis is an automotive technician copilot built with Meta glasses, a native iPhone companion, NVIDIA Nemotron, FastAPI, LlamaParse, FastEmbed and Qdrant.

- Preserve existing backend routes and iOS/frontend request contracts.
- Follow Meta's official CameraAccess implementation for registration, permission and capture lifecycle. Never invent SDK APIs.
- Use Nemotron for visual context and question interpretation. Technical values require exact, reviewed manual evidence and deterministic Python validation.
- Require explicit vehicle identity and relevant variants. Never fall back to another model/year or confuse oil/filter or fastener applications.
- Keep ordered procedure steps and warnings intact; a short voice answer must not omit required source instructions.
- New ingestion is pending review in an unaliased staging collection. Never auto-verify OCR. Preserve the deployed legacy collection.
- Read docs/qdrant-v2-migration.md before changing database configuration, review status or production aliases.
- Run backend tests and the relevant client build. Report actual results without promising unmeasured latency.
- Keep keys, photos, PDFs, database files, caches and review/backup exports outside Git.
